Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-07-2001||11:40 AM||||Butler Tire. here in Atlanta.. but any Enkei dealer. i had them drilled to the right bolt pattern by Rennsport Inc. in Lawrencville, Ga. for like $30 a wheel. (not RennTech the mercedes people, they are in florida) I had to order blanks. they were $10 more  I'll part with them and the tries for $1300 only have 2800miles on them. shipping included.. they have Dunlop W10s on them... <A HREF="http://www.butlertire.com" TARGET=_blank>www.butlertire.com</A>   -  well their site is being updated.. but check back soon..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>oh Enkei Phalnex   <A HREF="http://www.enkei.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enkei.com</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-07-2001||11:44 AM||||    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst_side_1.jpg">     <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst_qtr_1.jpg">     <P><BR>just had to taunt...      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thanks i appreciate the complements! <P>oh wheels are $330 each (their suggested retail prices are GROSSLY inflated).. tires were $115ea front and $135ea rear.. <P>crappy.. had the wrong link...<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">     <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||02-07-2001||05:39 PM||||Hey Trav, what's up with that exhaust tip? it's huge looking...ah ya know I'm just busting your genitals. But it seriously looks like there's only one there. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||02-08-2001||03:33 AM||||there is only one exhaust tip there.  After testing a few different setups he found that the single in/single out ?flowmaster? gave the most power.  right?||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-08-2001||08:18 AM||||yep.. after testing the stock unit, an ocelot, a flowmaster 40series cross flow, a 40 series single in single out, and now this brullen the single in/out laid down the best HP and TQ numbers. the velocity of the gases aren't changed as much as with the crossflow units and this aids in scavaging gases out of the heads. yeah it's a big tip    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    but it's not nearly as ricey as the pics look.. it's NOT loud or sticking WAY out. and it's a satin finish stainless not polished to not draw attention. and it's functional.. a straight cut off piece of 2.5" pipe just looks crap tastic... so i opted for the 3.5" tip.. the SE has a 4" tip.. it's not ricey either... Functional and subtle.. how can a huge tip be subtle.. give it a satin finish and people don't really pay it much attention.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
